.Dd August 27, 2026
.Dt C4C 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm c4c
.Nd compile C4 sources
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl h
.Op Fl d Ar dump
.Op Fl g Ar debug
.Op Fl I Ar dir | Fl I Cm -
.Op Fl O Ar level
.Op Fl o Ar file
.Op Fl T Ar triplet
.Op Fl t Ar src-type
.Ar source
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
program compiles a
.Em singular
.Ar source
file as C4 into an object file. It can also stop midway and dump various other
internal representations of the same source file.

The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d Ar dump
Stop after creating
.Ar dump
state and dump it, instead of compiling until the object file. Possible values
are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "AST"
.It AST
Dump the parsed abstract syntax tree of the C4 source. This is an unspecified,
but mostly human readable representation of the source code.
.It IR
Dump the generated LLVM IR of the C4 source. This is mostly useful for debugging
the compiler itself as this is far removed from the original source.
.It ASM
.Em It is currently not implemented.
It would dump the target assembly representation of the source code. This is
even more removed from the source than the aforementioned IR.
.El
.It Fl g Ar debug
Enables a debugging feature that helps debugging either the compiler, the
compiled source, or both. There are various values valid for
.Ar debug
documented in
.Xr c4c-debug 7 .
.It Fl h
Print short usage information and exit 100.
.It Fl I Ar dir
Add
.Ar dir
as a search path when resolving libraries. If the special value
.Cm -
is used, the search path is cleared instead. This removes system paths as well.
.It Fl O Ar level
Sets the optimization
The accepted levels are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "0"
.It Cm 0
The default value \(en no optimization is performed.
.It Cm 1 | 2 | 3
Perform optimizations for making the code faster. Higher levels are more
aggressive, possibly at the cost of code-size.
.It Cm s
Perform optimizations for making the code smaller. Balances performance with
code size, but prefers size.
.It Cm z
Perform optimizations for making the code smaller. Radically reduces the code at
the possibly cost of considerable performance.
.El
.It Fl o Ar file
Set the output to
.Ar file .
Defaults to the source's filename with the suffix replaced to
.Qq .o
if not set.
.It Fl T Ar triplet
Sets the target triplet for LLVM. See their documentation as to what it means.
.Pq Link in Sx SEE ALSO .
.It Fl t Ar src-type
Sets the source's type to
.Ar src-type
for this compilation. See
.Sx Source type
as to what this means. The accepted values are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width lib
.It Cm exec | Cm entry
Compile this source as an executable entrypoint and produce a
.Sy _c4_main
function.
.It Cm lib
Compile this source as an auxiliary library source.
.El
.El

.Ss Source type
Since C4 does not have a deliberate executable entrypoint other than falling
into the code and start executing, all compiled sources must be compiled as
either
.Em the single
entrypoint or auxiliary library sources. Failing in either direction
.Pq multiple entrypoints or all libraries
will cause linker failure. If using the bundled
.Xr c4ld 1
linker, it has extra error messages to help make sense of these situations.

There is an autodetection algorithm: if there are top-level expressions that
are not declarations or definitions of functions, then it is compiled as an
executable entrypoint, otherwise as library source. Note that library does not
mean as a separately compiled library archive as produced by
.Xr c4ar 1 ,
but a source file
.Ic use Ns -d
.Pq Xr c4-use 7
by the entrypoint to do its job.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
On success,
.Nm
exits 0. In case of failure, the following are used:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It 1
Invalid C4 source with syntactic or semantic errors.
.It 100
Invalid invocation. Flags or arguments malformed or missing.
.It 101
Unexpected error. Please file a bug report.
.It 111
General runtime error: syscall failure or LLVM error.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Lk https://clang.llvm.org/docs/CrossCompilation.html#target-triple LLVM Triplet usage ,
.Xr c4ar 1 ,
.Xr c4ld 1 ,
.Xr c4c-debug 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An András Bodor Aq Mt bodand@proton.me
.Sh BUGS
Currently color output cannot be turned off.

The type autodetection algorithm is not yet implemented. Every source must
manually be compiled with
.Fl t Ar lib
passed to not have an entrypoint.